# The windowed client as NATIVE arm64, via HashLink/C.
#
# HL's JIT has no arm64 backend, so `hl playground.hl` cannot work on Apple
# Silicon (the community's options are Rosetta or a WIP arm64 JIT). HL/C sidesteps
# the JIT entirely: Haxe emits C, and clang compiles it against the arm64 libhl
# and .hdll natives Homebrew already ships.
#
#   haxe build-hlc.hxml && ./bin/hlc/playground
-main Main
-cp src
-cp ../../../../colyseus-haxe/src
-lib heaps
-lib hlsdl
-lib colyseus-websocket
-lib tink_http
-hl bin/hlc/main.c
